WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.734 --> 00:00:01.968
- I don't think I,

00:00:01.968 --> 00:00:03.103
I still don't think
I am conservative

00:00:03.103 --> 00:00:05.105 align:start size:84% position:16%
in the older
meaning of the word.

00:00:06.272 --> 00:00:08.508
I'm definitely not, you know,

00:00:08.508 --> 00:00:12.045 align:start size:97% position:3%
if you went and read some
particular political treatise

00:00:12.045 --> 00:00:14.714 align:start position:0%
on conservatism, I'm gonna
disagree with quite a bit of it.

00:00:14.714 --> 00:00:17.550 align:start size:84% position:16%
At the same time, I
find a lot of sympathy

00:00:17.550 --> 00:00:20.687
for the arguments of
preserving something

00:00:20.687 --> 00:00:23.490 align:start size:94% position:6%
that is worth preserving,
or conserving that.

00:00:23.490 --> 00:00:25.592 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, yeah, I was
definitely not a radical,

00:00:25.592 --> 00:00:28.028
definitely kind of
middle of the road,

00:00:28.028 --> 00:00:32.699 align:start size:94% position:6%
average, everyday
Liberal left kind of guy.

00:00:32.699 --> 00:00:36.436
And I was genuinely, like
you said, apprehensive,

00:00:36.436 --> 00:00:38.004
is kind of an understatement,

00:00:38.004 --> 00:00:41.141
to work with conservatives
in any significant regard.

00:00:42.375 --> 00:00:44.577
Which has been really an
interesting experience,

00:00:44.577 --> 00:00:46.012 align:start size:84% position:16%
because they're
exactly the opposite

00:00:46.012 --> 00:00:47.380
of what the leftist propaganda

00:00:47.380 --> 00:00:48.882
had told me they would be like.

00:00:48.882 --> 00:00:52.419
(easy going digital music)

00:00:55.688 --> 00:00:57.090 align:start size:84% position:16% line:0%
- I'm Dave Rubin,
and joining me today

00:00:57.090 --> 00:00:59.459 line:0%
is the founder of
New Discourses,

00:00:59.459 --> 00:01:00.794 line:0%
and the co-author

00:01:00.794 --> 00:01:04.197 align:start size:88% position:13% line:0%
of "Cynical Theories,
How Activist Scholarship

00:01:04.197 --> 00:01:08.368 align:start size:97% position:3%
Made Everything About Race,
Gender, and Identity."

00:01:08.368 --> 00:01:10.770
James Lindsay, welcome
back to The Rubin Report.

00:01:10.770 --> 00:01:12.338
- Hey, Dave. Good
to see you, man.

00:01:12.338 --> 00:01:13.807
- It's good to see you.

00:01:13.807 --> 00:01:16.309
You know, I didn't realize
until we booked you for today

00:01:16.309 --> 00:01:17.544
that you've been on the show

00:01:17.544 --> 00:01:19.813
a couple of times but
only in panel form.

00:01:19.813 --> 00:01:23.083 align:start size:84% position:16%
You've never been
on as a solo entity.

00:01:23.083 --> 00:01:23.917
- That's right.
- This is as good

00:01:23.917 --> 00:01:25.151
as it gets, huh?

00:01:25.151 --> 00:01:27.720
- Yeah. Well, here
I am to change that.

00:01:27.720 --> 00:01:28.988
- Here you are.

00:01:28.988 --> 00:01:31.124
So actually the first
time that I had you on

00:01:31.124 --> 00:01:34.327
I had you on with our
friend Peter Boghossian

00:01:34.327 --> 00:01:35.728
who everybody knows.

00:01:35.728 --> 00:01:38.331
And when the show ended,
that was probably about

00:01:38.331 --> 00:01:41.000 align:start size:94% position:6%
it's gotta be a good
three years already or so.

00:01:41.000 --> 00:01:42.669
And when the show ended

00:01:42.669 --> 00:01:44.804 align:start size:88% position:13%
I think you sort of
still thought you could

00:01:44.804 --> 00:01:47.774
maybe modify some of this
stuff from within the left.

00:01:47.774 --> 00:01:49.609 align:start size:84% position:16%
And I had kind of
shifted a little bit.

00:01:49.609 --> 00:01:51.277 align:start size:84% position:16%
And when the cameras
went off, I said,

00:01:51.277 --> 00:01:52.479
"Well, you know, James,

00:01:52.479 --> 00:01:54.280
I sense that the conservatives

00:01:54.280 --> 00:01:55.849
are gonna start liking you,

00:01:55.849 --> 00:01:56.983
and you might want to go in
that direction a little bit,

00:01:56.983 --> 00:01:58.251
because I think you're gonna

00:01:58.251 --> 00:01:59.819
find fertile ground
for these ideas."

00:01:59.819 --> 00:02:01.321
And I sense you were
kind of were like,

00:02:01.321 --> 00:02:04.324
"Ah, I don't want to
do that just yet."

00:02:04.324 --> 00:02:05.592
That's three years ago.

00:02:05.592 --> 00:02:07.560
And man, it's been
a wild ride, huh?

00:02:07.560 --> 00:02:11.698 align:start size:84% position:16% line:0%
- Yeah. It's been
quite the few years.

00:02:11.698 --> 00:02:16.136 align:start size:94% position:6% line:0%
You were very largely
right about that analysis.

00:02:16.136 --> 00:02:17.370
- This interview is over.

00:02:17.370 --> 00:02:18.037
That's all I needed
to hear from you.

00:02:18.037 --> 00:02:19.506
- There you go.

00:02:19.506 --> 00:02:20.573 align:start size:94% position:6%
Dave Rubin was right.
- You were right. (laughs)

00:02:20.573 --> 00:02:22.642
- You know, put it on your book.

00:02:22.642 --> 00:02:24.244
- Yeah. So, all right.

00:02:24.244 --> 00:02:25.411
I didn't need the
you were right.

00:02:25.411 --> 00:02:26.279
But I think it does-

00:02:26.279 --> 00:02:27.480
- No, really though.

00:02:27.480 --> 00:02:29.782 align:start size:88% position:13%
- But it does illustrate
a certain something.

00:02:29.782 --> 00:02:32.685
So before we even go
into that part of it

00:02:32.685 --> 00:02:36.055
about sort of looking to
the right for new bridges.

00:02:36.055 --> 00:02:38.424 align:start size:94% position:6%
When did you get
interested in all of this?

00:02:38.424 --> 00:02:40.360
You seem to be the main guy

00:02:40.360 --> 00:02:41.728
covering critical race theory,

00:02:41.728 --> 00:02:42.996
you've been warning
about it forever.

00:02:42.996 --> 00:02:45.899
You're taking the
heat for doing so.

00:02:45.899 --> 00:02:48.501
When did this even
get on your radar?

00:02:48.501 --> 00:02:50.537 align:start size:97% position:3%
- You know, it hit my radar,
it was very interesting.

00:02:50.537 --> 00:02:52.071
I didn't know what
I was looking at,

00:02:52.071 --> 00:02:55.108
obviously, seven
or eight years ago.

00:02:55.108 --> 00:02:57.043
But I got involved
in a conversation

00:02:57.043 --> 00:02:58.311
with a number of people.

00:02:58.311 --> 00:03:01.181
The conversation
was about a topic

00:03:01.181 --> 00:03:02.582
that nobody finds controversial,

00:03:02.582 --> 00:03:04.117
whatsoever, Affirmative Action.

00:03:05.985 --> 00:03:08.354
I was talking with a blue
collar friend of mine,

00:03:08.354 --> 00:03:10.523 align:start size:84% position:16%
and he's talking
about his experience,

00:03:10.523 --> 00:03:14.294 align:start size:84% position:16%
and the probably
well-founded suspicion

00:03:14.294 --> 00:03:17.497
that his boss was
a diversity hire,

00:03:17.497 --> 00:03:20.033 align:start size:94% position:6%
as opposed to somebody who
was actually qualified.

00:03:20.033 --> 00:03:21.467 align:start size:88% position:13%
And in fact, he was
talking about how there

00:03:21.467 --> 00:03:23.469 align:start size:88% position:13%
had been some incidents
where people have

00:03:23.469 --> 00:03:25.104
been put physically at risk,

00:03:25.104 --> 00:03:27.006
since he actually
works in a factory.

00:03:27.006 --> 00:03:28.474 align:start size:88% position:13%
And there were a
number of other people.

00:03:28.474 --> 00:03:29.876
And if memory serves,

00:03:29.876 --> 00:03:32.445
a younger white woman
was present as well.

00:03:32.445 --> 00:03:34.881
And she pointed out that,

00:03:36.216 --> 00:03:38.318
there was no need
to tell this story,

00:03:38.318 --> 00:03:42.388 align:start size:88% position:13%
because white men's
stories have been told.

00:03:42.388 --> 00:03:45.592
And I kind of interjected,
and I said, "Now hold on.

00:03:46.960 --> 00:03:49.262 align:start size:94% position:6%
I get where you're
coming from historically.

00:03:49.262 --> 00:03:52.365
However, we're in a
new circumstance now.

00:03:52.365 --> 00:03:54.400
And he's trying to tell
his actual experience

00:03:54.400 --> 00:03:55.768
with what he's dealing with.

00:03:55.768 --> 00:03:57.704
And so the idea that, you know

00:03:57.704 --> 00:03:59.606
white working class
people are going

00:03:59.606 --> 00:04:01.140 align:start size:84% position:16%
to be put underneath
the dominion

00:04:01.140 --> 00:04:03.776
of possibly incompetent bosses

00:04:03.776 --> 00:04:05.979
that were hired for
Affirmative Action,

00:04:05.979 --> 00:04:09.649 align:start size:84% position:16%
or diversity reasons
is a new story.

00:04:09.649 --> 00:04:12.518
And we should be telling that
story, and hearing this story

00:04:12.518 --> 00:04:13.720
and seeing what there is to get

00:04:13.720 --> 00:04:15.355
to the best possible result."

00:04:15.355 --> 00:04:18.224
And it was just like ice.

00:04:18.224 --> 00:04:22.662 align:start size:84% position:16%
"His story has
already been told."

00:04:22.662 --> 00:04:26.165 align:start size:88% position:13%
And I was like, there's
something bad wrong

00:04:26.165 --> 00:04:27.634
in that attitude.

00:04:27.634 --> 00:04:30.103 align:start size:97% position:3%
That was the very first
kind of tip of the iceberg.

00:04:30.103 --> 00:04:31.738 align:start size:84% position:16%
And then as you know,
we were involved

00:04:31.738 --> 00:04:34.073 align:start size:84% position:16%
in the new Atheist
movement, Peter and I.

00:04:34.073 --> 00:04:37.176 align:start size:88% position:13%
And our heroes, who
were friends previously,

00:04:37.176 --> 00:04:40.813 align:start size:97% position:3%
I think with both of us who
largely don't like us anymore.

00:04:40.813 --> 00:04:43.449
We're getting accused
of things like sexism,

00:04:43.449 --> 00:04:46.486 align:start position:0%
and sometimes racism for charges
that didn't make any sense.

00:04:46.486 --> 00:04:48.321 align:start size:94% position:6%
And that's where I started
to hear these words

00:04:48.321 --> 00:04:50.890
systemic racism,
systemic sexism,

00:04:50.890 --> 00:04:54.527
and to start to connect
that to certain stories,

00:04:54.527 --> 00:04:55.795
aren't allowed to be told,

00:04:55.795 --> 00:04:57.697
whereas other stories
have to be amplified,

00:04:57.697 --> 00:04:59.399
or centered, or whatever.

00:04:59.399 --> 00:05:01.200
And that's where
I really started

00:05:01.200 --> 00:05:03.069
to get concerned and
nervous about this,

00:05:03.069 --> 00:05:06.572 align:start size:94% position:6%
as early as 2000, probably
'14 at the latest.

00:05:08.041 --> 00:05:10.977
And Peter and I started to
talk about it then really.

00:05:10.977 --> 00:05:13.046
- So you and Pete
were ahead on this.

00:05:13.046 --> 00:05:15.148
And then when did,
when were you like,

00:05:15.148 --> 00:05:19.285
"Okay, well, I either want to
make a living dissecting this,

00:05:19.285 --> 00:05:22.388 align:start size:97% position:3%
or I'm gonna write a book
about this, or I need to..."

00:05:22.388 --> 00:05:24.724
You know, this isn't
a fun thing for anyone

00:05:24.724 --> 00:05:26.326
to be involved in
at a certain level,

00:05:26.326 --> 00:05:28.428 align:start size:94% position:6%
especially the way
you're involved in on it.

00:05:28.428 --> 00:05:29.796 align:start size:84% position:16%
Because you're always
gonna be accused

00:05:29.796 --> 00:05:32.365
of being the worst
things at all times.

00:05:32.365 --> 00:05:34.067
When did you make that shift?

00:05:34.067 --> 00:05:37.003
- Yeah, so Peter and I
decided to fatefully,

00:05:37.003 --> 00:05:40.473
in early 2017, to
write a hoax paper

00:05:40.473 --> 00:05:43.142 align:start size:94% position:6%
targeting gender studies,
as we've discussed.

00:05:43.142 --> 00:05:46.245
And we wrote, "The Conceptual
Penis is a Social Construct."

00:05:46.245 --> 00:05:48.014
That was its own little scandal.

00:05:48.948 --> 00:05:50.216
But we spiked a football

00:05:50.216 --> 00:05:51.751 align:start size:84% position:16%
I don't think we had
a right to spike.

00:05:51.751 --> 00:05:54.454 align:start size:94% position:6%
We said, "We proved
gender studies is bogus."

00:05:54.454 --> 00:05:56.622
I don't think we actually
had the evidence for that

00:05:56.622 --> 00:06:00.626 align:start size:97% position:3%
given the poor quality of
the journal that accepted it.

00:06:00.626 --> 00:06:02.562
And this created
some controversy.

00:06:02.562 --> 00:06:04.664 align:start size:97% position:3%
So Peter and I, being Peter
and I, talked about it,

00:06:04.664 --> 00:06:07.233
and we decided maybe we
should write more papers.

00:06:07.233 --> 00:06:09.669
And so we recruited
Helen, fatefully,

00:06:09.669 --> 00:06:12.438
and we set a set
out on writing the,

00:06:12.438 --> 00:06:14.574 align:start size:88% position:13%
"Papers of the Grievance
Studies Affair."

00:06:14.574 --> 00:06:18.678
And that's where by the
end of the year, 2017,

00:06:18.678 --> 00:06:20.580 align:start size:81% position:19%
well into that
project, you know,

00:06:20.580 --> 00:06:22.548 align:start size:97% position:3%
we're actually reading
their literature in detail.

00:06:22.548 --> 00:06:25.184
We're not just trying to
pull jokes by that point.

00:06:25.184 --> 00:06:27.387
We're getting feedback
from academic journals

00:06:27.387 --> 00:06:29.155 align:start size:97% position:3%
saying these are the
things that you've written.

00:06:29.155 --> 00:06:31.924
For example, like this
idea that you have to

00:06:31.924 --> 00:06:35.328
kind of abuse students in the
name of progressive ideology,

00:06:35.328 --> 00:06:38.498 align:start size:97% position:3%
under a progressive stack
with experiential reparations.

00:06:38.498 --> 00:06:40.767 align:start size:88% position:13%
Is like the mistake they
told us that we made,

00:06:40.767 --> 00:06:42.468 align:start size:94% position:6%
they said white fragility
is the right idea,

00:06:42.468 --> 00:06:45.405
but the mistake you've made
is centering compassion.

00:06:45.405 --> 00:06:47.140
You have to center discomfort.

00:06:47.140 --> 00:06:49.542
Otherwise you might refocus on,

00:06:49.542 --> 00:06:51.744
or recenter the needs
of the privileged.

00:06:51.744 --> 00:06:54.514 align:start size:97% position:3%
And that's where I remember
getting that feedback,

00:06:54.514 --> 00:06:56.048 align:start size:81% position:19%
and looking at
this and thinking,

00:06:56.048 --> 00:06:59.352
that it's like pulling back a
tarp and finding a dead body.

00:06:59.352 --> 00:07:01.354
Like something really
bad is happening here.

00:07:01.354 --> 00:07:03.022
And as I've gone on
and I've read more

00:07:03.022 --> 00:07:04.857 align:start size:84% position:16%
of their literature
over the years,

00:07:04.857 --> 00:07:06.692 align:start size:88% position:13%
especially when I first
read a book called,

00:07:06.692 --> 00:07:08.795
"Is Everyone Really Equal?"

00:07:08.795 --> 00:07:11.964 align:start size:88% position:13%
In probably the middle,
early part of 2019,

00:07:11.964 --> 00:07:14.700
which is written by Özlem
Sensoy and Robin DiAngelo.

00:07:14.700 --> 00:07:16.969 align:start size:84% position:16%
It's an education
book written in 2012.

00:07:16.969 --> 00:07:19.305 align:start size:84% position:16%
Now it's like, wow,
this isn't a dead body

00:07:19.305 --> 00:07:21.107
under a tarp, it's a mass grave.

00:07:21.107 --> 00:07:22.975
And at that point
it's like, okay

00:07:22.975 --> 00:07:24.710
I have to basically dedicate

00:07:25.845 --> 00:07:28.748 align:start size:88% position:13%
most of my time and
energy to exposing this.

00:07:28.748 --> 00:07:30.216
It's not about making money,

00:07:30.216 --> 00:07:31.751 align:start size:94% position:6%
in fact, I didn't make
any money for a long time.

00:07:31.751 --> 00:07:34.053
My wife actually literally
supported us completely,

00:07:34.053 --> 00:07:36.856
because she also saw
how important it was

00:07:36.856 --> 00:07:39.792
for somebody to research
this and speak up about it

00:07:39.792 --> 00:07:42.595 align:start size:97% position:3%
to say, "You know, something
is badly off the rails."

00:07:42.595 --> 00:07:45.097
That these ideas exist
isn't itself a problem,

00:07:45.097 --> 00:07:48.301
but that they're
institutionalizing
is a big problem,

00:07:48.301 --> 00:07:52.004 align:start size:84% position:16%
that they're capturing
a political party
is a big problem.

00:07:52.004 --> 00:07:53.906
And so I didn't make any money

00:07:53.906 --> 00:07:55.575 align:start size:94% position:6%
for a very long time
actually working on this.

00:07:55.575 --> 00:07:57.443 align:start size:84% position:16%
And I started to
research and I noticed

00:07:57.443 --> 00:08:00.146 align:start size:84% position:16%
how often they use
the words, revolution.

00:08:00.146 --> 00:08:01.614
Equity is not enough, this is in

00:08:01.614 --> 00:08:03.916
a mathematics education paper.

00:08:03.916 --> 00:08:05.518
Maybe equity isn't enough,

00:08:05.518 --> 00:08:07.553 align:start size:84% position:16%
maybe what we needed
was a revolution.

00:08:07.553 --> 00:08:09.755 align:start size:84% position:16%
And I thought
something really bad

00:08:09.755 --> 00:08:11.424
is at the end of this rainbow.

00:08:11.424 --> 00:08:13.893
And that's where
it's everything,

00:08:13.893 --> 00:08:15.962
it's all I do now, is
something really bad

00:08:15.962 --> 00:08:17.897
is at the end of this
rainbow, let's stop it.

00:08:17.897 --> 00:08:20.933
- Yeah. That's why I think
your story is so interesting,

00:08:20.933 --> 00:08:24.570 align:start size:97% position:3%
because it seems like you
just kept peeling the onion.

00:08:24.570 --> 00:08:26.205
And it kept going
deeper, and deeper,

00:08:26.205 --> 00:08:28.140
and getting in some
ways more perverse.

00:08:28.140 --> 00:08:30.076 align:start size:97% position:3%
I mean, for the people
that didn't see the episode

00:08:30.076 --> 00:08:32.612
that I did with you
and Pete in studio

00:08:32.612 --> 00:08:34.013 align:start size:84% position:16%
where you talk about
the Sokal hoax.

00:08:34.013 --> 00:08:35.281
I mean, in essence
what you're saying

00:08:35.281 --> 00:08:37.450 align:start size:84% position:16%
is you wrote something
to be nonsensical,

00:08:37.450 --> 00:08:40.152 align:start size:84% position:16%
and yet it wasn't even
nonsensical enough.

00:08:40.152 --> 00:08:44.223 align:start size:97% position:3%
That's the really bizarre part
of the whole thing, right?

00:08:44.223 --> 00:08:46.092
I mean, you couldn't,
you tried to make up

00:08:46.092 --> 00:08:48.194 align:start size:84% position:16%
as nonsensical
thing as you could.

00:08:48.194 --> 00:08:49.695
- Yeah, and that
was the thing we,

00:08:49.695 --> 00:08:51.197 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean that was one of the
things that clued us in

00:08:51.197 --> 00:08:52.632
that there was a problem.

00:08:52.632 --> 00:08:54.066 align:start size:94% position:6%
And it wasn't like finding
a dead body so much,

00:08:54.066 --> 00:08:58.471
as it was, something's
bad off with academia,

00:08:58.471 --> 00:08:59.872
is that every time
we'd write a paper

00:08:59.872 --> 00:09:01.707 align:start size:97% position:3%
and we're all proud of
ourselves for how ridiculous,

00:09:01.707 --> 00:09:03.809 align:start size:94% position:6%
or horrifying, or whatever
it happened to be,

00:09:03.809 --> 00:09:05.811 align:start size:94% position:6%
we would find something
in the existing literature

00:09:05.811 --> 00:09:07.380 align:start size:84% position:16%
that actually
already went further.

00:09:07.380 --> 00:09:09.148
Like we wrote one paper arguing

00:09:09.148 --> 00:09:13.319
that the real reason that men
participate in combat sports

00:09:13.319 --> 00:09:15.121
like Brazilian jujitsu,

