that's very useful.

00:11:42.168 --> 00:11:43.436
I can use this.

00:11:43.436 --> 00:11:45.071 align:start size:84% position:16%
And so we took out the
word, our movement,

00:11:45.071 --> 00:11:46.572
he didn't call it
Nazis at the time,

00:11:46.572 --> 00:11:48.474 align:start size:84% position:16%
he called it our
movement in the book.

00:11:48.474 --> 00:11:49.975
And we took out the
words, our movement,

00:11:49.975 --> 00:11:51.610
and I just replaced it with
intersectional feminism,

00:11:51.610 --> 00:11:55.147 align:start position:0%
literally just find and replace
on like Word or whatever.

00:11:55.147 --> 00:11:57.416 align:start size:97% position:3%
And then it was like, okay,
now I read through it.

00:11:57.416 --> 00:11:58.684
And I changed the sentences

00:11:58.684 --> 00:12:00.252
so that they're not
complete nonsense,

00:12:00.252 --> 00:12:01.754
that since we changed words.

00:12:01.754 --> 00:12:04.356
And then it was like layers of
let's work in some research,

00:12:04.356 --> 00:12:06.625 align:start size:84% position:16%
let's work in a little
bit of citations.

00:12:06.625 --> 00:12:07.960
Let's pull from Bell Hooks,

00:12:07.960 --> 00:12:10.429 align:start size:84% position:16%
let's pull from these
angry feminists.

00:12:10.429 --> 00:12:13.632
And we came up with this
idea that there's a type

00:12:13.632 --> 00:12:15.534
of feminism called
choice feminism,

00:12:15.534 --> 00:12:18.504 align:start size:84% position:16%
that women enacting
their own free choices

00:12:18.504 --> 00:12:20.506
